  "notes": "Themes searched: economy (land, wages, bonded labour, unions, poverty), government (representation, local governance, police impunity, state duty), society (patriarchy, marriage, divorce, inheritance, intersectionality, knowledge), world (UN treaties, Durban, Beijing), liberty, culture (religion, conversion), ecology, technology and means; most had no stated position. Adherents differ on 'Dalit patriarchy' (Guru and Chakravarti accept it, Arya rejects it) and on the uniform civil code (Rege records a Bahujan Mahila strand that opposes it; no source found here states the other side, so it is null). Not opened: Guru's 1995 EPW essay, Chakravarti's Gendering Caste, Dalit Women Speak Out (403 or no full text), the Delhi Declaration text, Ambedkar's Annihilation of Caste was downloaded but no answer rests on it."
